course: dictionary
lesson: 15683
title: Words for people who keep time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A timekeeper is a person who keeps track of time. In a race or game, the timekeeper watches the clock, often with a stopwatch, and says when time is up. «Mia was the timekeeper for the sports day races.» Mia watched the clock, so timekeeper must mean the person who keeps track of time.
explain: Timekeeper can also describe someone who is always on time. «She is an excellent timekeeper» means she is never late. The words around the word show which meaning is right: a race or stopwatch tells you it is about timing, and being on time tells you it is about punctuality.
explain: A timekeeper can also be a clock or watch. If a sentence talks about how accurately something keeps time, the word may mean the clock itself. Always ask: is this a person doing a job, or a thing that shows the time? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A timekeeper is a person who keeps track of time in a game, race or event.
fact: Timekeepers often use a stopwatch and say when time is up.
fact: «A good timekeeper» means someone who is always on time.
fact: «Official timekeeper» means the person in charge of timing an event.
fact: A timekeeper can also be a clock or watch that keeps time accurately.
exercise: «The teacher chose Sam as the timekeeper for the debate.» What does timekeeper mean here? | A person who always wins the debate | A loud clock on the wall | *A person who times each speech | A pupil who is always late
exercise: «She is an excellent timekeeper, never late for training.» What does timekeeper mean here? | A coach who gives out medals | A stopwatch used in races | Someone who keeps the score | *Someone who is always on time
exercise: Which word could describe a clock that keeps time very accurately? | *timekeeper | sprinter | umpire | captain
test: «The official timekeeper stopped the race at the finish line.» What does official timekeeper suggest? | *The person in charge of timing the race | A player who scores the goals | The winner's coach | The fastest runner in the race
test: «Jo was a poor timekeeper and often arrived after the bell.» What does poor timekeeper mean? | *Someone who is often late | Someone who never speaks in class | Someone who rings the school bell | Someone who keeps very good time
exam: Which sentence uses timekeeper to mean a clock or watch? | «The timekeeper wrote down each runner's time.» | «The timekeeper blew the whistle to start the race.» | «She is an excellent timekeeper and is never late.» | *«The old timekeeper on the wall has kept perfect time for fifty years.»
